	(text "Isolated interface: digital isolator, set-point DAC, readback ADC"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 18.0 22.0 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "JetBrains Mono")
				(size 4.5 4.5)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 40 90 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "31fe6bd7-f4ff-5197-925c-68b3af66b9f6")
	)
	(text "SPI crosses the barrier. The DAC and ADC carry their own references, so no precision reference or trimmer is needed."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 18.0 26.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "JetBrains Mono")
				(size 2.0 2.0)
				(italic yes)
				(color 70 70 70 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "f295078f-7542-5c6d-8f53-befdf97accaa")
	)
	(text "ISOLATION BARRIER"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 113.62 89.94 90)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "JetBrains Mono")
				(size 2.0 2.0)
				(bold yes)
				(color 200 0 0 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "0c435432-abd8-5742-a1ae-1153453b504c")
	)
	(text "Side 1 = USB side after the J10/J11 cable (3.3 V_LK), side 2 = analog\n(5 V). Five channels cross, MISO comes back. CA-IS3761HW (the H suffix) and\nthe TI ISO7761 are pin-compatible; both have outputs that default HIGH\nwhen side 1 is unpowered or an input floats: chip selects stay\nde-asserted and LOAD_OFF_ISO is asserted, so the load is OFF until\nfirmware says otherwise. R21-R23 (on this board) give the same guarantee\nwith the MCU in reset or the cable unplugged. 11 ns delay: SPI <= 2 MHz."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 57.02 173.94 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "JetBrains Mono")
				(size 2.0 2.0)
				(color 40 40 40 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "c25e0ba0-3df0-5190-ba0a-d05fe784b470")
	)
	(text "A   Digital isolator"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 48.99 55.67 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "JetBrains Mono")
				(size 2.5 2.5)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 50 120 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "94f89175-1237-5c1a-be8f-f3da92004f8b")
	)
	(text "12 bit, internal 2.048 V reference, gain 2: 0 - 4.095 V in 1 mV steps.\nA: LOAD_CTRL, 2.5 A per volt = 2.44 mA per LSB. B: CV_SET in VSEN volts.\nBoth outputs are 0 V after power-up (POR shutdown): no EEPROM surprise\nlike the MCP4725."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 245.02 131.94 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "JetBrains Mono")
				(size 2.0 2.0)
				(color 40 40 40 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "8e9f297e-7987-5165-97e5-72c494b4f003")
	)
	(text "B   Set-point DAC: A = current ceiling, B = CV voltage"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 240.76 58.21 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(face "JetBrains Mono")
				(size 2.5 2.5)
				(bold yes)
				(color 0 50 120 1)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "4160361f-7826-587e-9a02-a1757bd4eb43")
	)
	(text "AIN0 ISEN (0.30 V/A), AIN1 VSEN (0.049 V/V), AIN2 heatsink NTC, AIN3 the\nlive V_SET node (PGA +-256 mV): shows what the loops really get after OTP,\nOFF, KILL or CV pull it down. Internal reference 0.01 %, 7 ppm/K, 860 SPS,\nplus a die temperature sensor."
